infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Reading a process exit code: 128 + N decodes the signal
  desc From a clean drain down to the forced kill
  lists
    - label 0 — clean exit
      desc Loop drained on its own; shutdown finished before the deadline.
    - label 130 = 128 + 2 — SIGINT
      desc Ctrl-C in the foreground; the 128 + signal-number contract.
    - label 143 = 128 + 15 — SIGTERM
      desc Polite stop (k8s, docker stop, systemd) that no handler caught.
    - label 137 = 128 + 9 — SIGKILL
      desc The hammer: grace period expired, kernel forced the kill.
theme
  palette #10b981 #6366f1 #f59e0b #f43f5e
